><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251112101134+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="fd14fe00-0cde-406d-95b5-ee0f027f0fab" date="D:20251112101134+10'00'" name="7f258a43-2dfb-4a73-99b5-0534408875e4" icon="Comment" page="2" rect="41.646713,97.161072,65.646713,121.161072" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: yes there were practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="2" rect="595.276001,29.161072,779.276001,121.161072"
/></text
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251112101143+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="fd14fe00-0cde-406d-95b5-ee0f027f0fab" date="D:20251112101146+10'00'" name="4a71307f-4f8c-4997-bd4c-93411a675840" icon="Comment" page="2" rect="41.646713,97.161072,65.646713,121.161072" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Detailed information about study participants facilitates immediate&#xD;and appropriate clinical translation. Certain tendinopathy&#xD;treatments might be more effective in specific patient&#xD;groups (athletic vs non-athletic,&#xD;older vs younger, presence of&#xD;comorbidities, etc). For example, eccentric exercise has high-level&#xD;evidence for the treatment of recreational male runners with mid-portion&#xD;Achilles tendinopathy,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>4 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>but this treatment&#xD;has been shown to be less effective for tendons other than the&#xD;Achilles,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>5 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>in-season&#xD;athletes,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>6 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>women,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>7 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>sedentary patients and&#xD;those with high body mass index.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>8 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This example highlights the&#xD;large number of relevant participant characteristics that may be&#xD;associated with treatment response that should be available to&#xD;clinicians and other researchers. It also highlights the challenges&#xD;represented by heterogeneous sample populations. Patients and&#xD;clinicians benefit from having the participant characteristics&#xD;clearly described in making management decisions.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>9</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="2" rect="595.276001,29.161072,779.276001,121.161072"
/></text
